{"title":"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b109bbad8ddff023f591be8a7ed806fdcc5938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 7, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is an arithmetic sequence with three terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c0e08c45ffc6a53d886e11870aa0206c258d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, 7, q, 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />, in that order, form an arithmetic sequence with four terms. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are consecutive terms in an arithmetic sequence, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This can be shown through the fact that if the common difference of the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f5579a35e7806e4e3092943f40d32b26f0c7dd57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb9b33440f21cfd6d81614c426dd96d1d9cdeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = b + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb041e215226925772e73d212a45a614f156f4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a + c}{2} = \\frac{b - d + b + d}{2} = \\frac{2b}{2} = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"39\" />. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2b9b46082286ae8e1436b4da04a9d505988407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7 + 13}{2} = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c34bee1486881c6559629433e9e54ec605eed1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = \\frac{20}{2} = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c17f79e5305765a296641b3198daf312f2f9c50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p + 10}{2} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1529307bd82c7143b94da9ff4120d6cb16ac8b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + 10 = 7 \\times 2 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b88a8bf91d3d913a1ff18ca257c5024756e466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 14 - 10 = \\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"138\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3123/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.488      1 2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    6.488      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37228:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060314 and revision id 287505. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}